  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🔥 Blood Elf Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Elegant sin'dorei names, a few with an apostrophe, and surnames of sun, flame and gold."
    },
    "intro": "Blood elves, the sin'dorei, are proud, elegant and a little vain, and their names show it: Kael'thas Sunstrider, Lor'themar Theron, Lady Liadrin, Halduron Brightwing. This **blood elf name generator** gives you sin'dorei first names, some with the apostrophe of Kael'thas and Lor'themar, and surnames full of sun, flame and gold.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How blood elf names work",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>First names</strong> are graceful and often long. Some are split by an apostrophe: Kael'thas, Lor'themar. Others aren't: Liadrin, Rommath, Halduron.</li><li><strong>Surnames</strong> are often English compounds about light, the sun or flight: Sunstrider, Windrunner, Brightwing. Some, like Theron, are single elven words.</li></ul><p>The surnames in this generator are new compounds in that style, leaning on the sun, flame and gold that suit Silvermoon.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "From high elves to blood elves",
        "content": "<p>The blood elves were once the <a href=\"high-elf-name-generator.html\">high elves</a>, the quel'dorei, of Quel'Thalas. After the Scourge destroyed much of their kingdom and corrupted the Sunwell, the survivors took a new name, sin'dorei, \"children of the blood\", in memory of their dead. Their city, Silvermoon, and the restored Sunwell are at the heart of their story.</p><p>That history is useful for naming: a blood elf old enough to remember Quel'Thalas before its fall might keep an older, gentler name, while one born after might choose something fiercer.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Getting a free name in WoW",
        "content": "<p>WoW names must be one word and unique on your realm, and can't include an apostrophe, so a name like Kael'dorin needs to become Kaeldorin in game. Use the full name with surname for roleplay.</p><p>For other Warcraft races, see the <a href=\"night-elf-name-generator.html\">Night Elf</a>, <a href=\"wow-troll-name-generator.html\">Troll</a> and <a href=\"wow-orc-name-generator.html\">Orc</a> name generators.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What does sin'dorei mean?",
        "answer": "\"Children of the blood\". The high elves took the name after the fall of Quel'Thalas, in memory of those who died."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can I use an apostrophe in a WoW name?",
        "answer": "No. WoW character names are a single word of letters only, so drop the apostrophe: Kael'dorin becomes Kaeldorin."
      },
      {
        "question": "Are blood elves the same as high elves?",
        "answer": "They were the same people. Most high elves became blood elves after Quel'Thalas fell; a few kept the old name, quel'dorei."
      }
    ]
  }
